      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-312879",
      ":question/problem": "In triangles $MNO$ and $UVW$, sides $MN^(\u2015)$ and $UV^(\u2015)$ each have measure $6$ and sides $MO^(\u2015)$ and $UW^(\u2015)$ each have measure $10$. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that triangle $MNO$ is congruent to triangle $UVW$?\n\n1. The length of $NO^(\u2015)$.\n2. The measures of $\u2220N$ and $\u2220V$ are equal.\n3. The lengths of $NO^(\u2015)$ and $VW^(\u2015)$ are equal.\n4. No additional information is needed."
