      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-313118",
      ":question/problem": "In triangles $MNO$ and $KLP$, sides $MN^(\u2015)$ and $KL^(\u2015)$ each have measure $7$, and sides $MO^(\u2015)$ and $KP^(\u2015)$ each have measure $10$. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that triangle $MNO$ is congruent to triangle $UVW$?\n\n1. The measure of $\u2220P$.\n2. The measures of $\u2220N$ and $\u2220L$ are equal.\n3. The measures of $\u2220M$ and $\u2220K$ are equal.\n4. No additional information is needed."
